IO-58: leave the initial stored volume out of "Total Inflow Volume"

massbal_open() starts each node's inflow accumulator NodeInflow[j] at the
node's initial volume, so that the per-node balance (NodeOutflow includes
the final volume) closes. writeNodeFlows() printed the same accumulator as
the Node Inflow Summary's "Total Inflow Volume", which the manual defines
as lateral inflow plus inflow from connecting links. Keep the node's
initial volume in its statistics and subtract it from the printed column.
The flow balance error, the node continuity ranking and the storage loss
percentages still use NodeInflow and do not change.

Requires: BND-19

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-58_swmm530.patch

